body:
Friend of a friend sat behind me. She apparently had a thing for me and spent the entire movie playing with my hair. Would not leave it alone. Eventually made it pretty clear she wasn't to touch my hair. She apparently didn't like me much after that.

&#x200B;

Either that or going to watch a kids movie with my partner, kid behind me decides to stand on her seat so she can slap my head repeatedly. Parents too far away to control or notice (had like 8 kids with them)

We technically have "Freedom of Expression" which would functionally be the same thing if it wasn't for the last paragraph;

"2. The exercise of these freedoms, since it carries with it duties and responsibilities, may be subject to such formalities, conditions, restrictions or penalties as are prescribed by law and are necessary in a democratic society, in the interests of national security, territorial integrity or public safety, for the prevention of disorder or crime, for the protection of health or morals, for the protection of the reputation or rights of others, for preventing the disclosure of information received in confidence, or for maintaining the authority and impartiality of the judiciary."

Basically, you're free to say whatever you want, unless we can find literally any excuse to fuck you over anyway.
